Generated with OpenSCAD version 2025.06.12.ai25773 (default CGAL engine).
Run bash scripts/vendor-libs.sh first. Copy the patched snap source into
.tmp-pst-n60q0/snap.scad, replacing its final demo invocation at line 128
with a comment. This prevents an extra directional snap contaminating
lite/full renders. Keep its include <BOSL2/std.scad> and module unchanged.
The per-variant wrapper is:
    include <snap.scad>
    openGridSnap(lite=LITE, directional=DIRECTIONAL, anchor=BOTTOM);
lite.scad: LITE=true, DIRECTIONAL=false
full.scad: LITE=false, DIRECTIONAL=false
directional.scad: LITE=true, DIRECTIONAL=true
full-directional.scad: LITE=false, DIRECTIONAL=true

Exact command pattern, run at repository root for each NAME above:
    OPENSCADPATH="$PWD/libs" openscad -o "$PWD/assets/opengrid-snap/mesh/NAME.stl" "$PWD/.tmp-pst-n60q0/NAME.scad"
Z=0 is the snap bottom. The original meshes have non-manifold nub-root
interfaces. They are reference surfaces, not watertight printing assets.

